# Read by GitHub ("Cite this repository") and by Zenodo, which takes the title, authors, version and licence of each
# archived release from this file.  Add the DOI Zenodo mints for a release to `identifiers` once it exists; the
# concept DOI (the one that always resolves to the latest version) goes in `doi`.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use imgstrip in your work, please cite the version you used, as below."
type: software
title: "imgstrip"
abstract: >-
  imgstrip removes metadata and hidden data from images by rebuilding each file from its decoded pixels, and verifies
  every output before releasing it: a strict structural walk that must account for every byte, then a re-decode
  that must match the intended pixels. JPEG, PNG, WebP, GIF, TIFF, BMP, HEIC/HEIF and AVIF, with optional scrubbers
  for pixel and DCT steganography and the camera sensor fingerprint, and optional C2PA Content Credentials.
authors:
  - family-names: "Sato"
    given-names: "Lloyd"
version: "2.0.1"
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/lloydsato/imgstrip"
url: "https://github.com/lloydsato/imgstrip"
keywords:
  - image sanitisation
  - metadata removal
  - content disarm and reconstruction
  - steganography
  - PRNU
  - privacy
references:
  - type: report
    title: "imgstrip: Sanitising Images by Rebuilding Them from Their Pixels, with Fail-Closed Verification of the Result"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Sato"
        given-names: "Lloyd"
    year: 2026
    month: 10
    notes: "Preprint describing imgstrip 1.2.4; the changes in 1.2.5 answer its findings (see CHANGELOG.md)."
